    <div class="card-body border-top">
		<p class="mb-0">Pasturebird is one of the premier pasture raised poultry producers in the world. What sets the brand apart? The time and dedication it devotes to nurturing each and every flock. Chicks begin their lives in a brooder, which replicates the warmth and comfort of a mother hen. When old enough to survive on their own, chickens are moved outdoors at about three weeks of age, where they live 24/7 in floorless mobile coops, which are rotated to fresh pasture daily. A breed-appropriate diet of grasses, seeds, insects and grains keeps chickens happy and healthy. All this TLC adds up to more nutrient-dense poultry and, thanks to grazing practices, rejuvenates both the soil and the environment.</p>
